# API Route Standards

## Route Handlers

- Use TypeScript for all API routes
- Implement proper HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE)
- Return consistent response formats
- Handle errors gracefully

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from 'next/server';

export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  try {
    const body = await request.json();
    
    // Validate input
    const validated = validateBookingData(body);
    
    // Business logic
    const booking = await createBooking(validated);
    
    return NextResponse.json(
      { success: true, data: booking },
      { status: 201 }
    );
  } catch (error) {
    if (error instanceof ValidationError) {
      return NextResponse.json(
        { success: false, error: error.message },
        { status: 400 }
      );
    }
    
    console.error('Booking creation failed:', error);
    return NextResponse.json(
      { success: false, error: 'Internal server error' },
      { status: 500 }
    );
  }
}
```

## Response Format

- Always use consistent response structure
- Include success/error status
- Provide meaningful error messages

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD - Consistent format
{
  success: true,
  data: { /* response data */ }
}

// ❌ BAD - Inconsistent
{ booking: {...} } // Sometimes
{ data: {...} }    // Other times
```

## Validation

- Validate all inputs at API boundary
- Use schema validation (Zod, Yup, etc.)
- Return 400 for validation errors

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

const bookingSchema = z.object({
  customerName: z.string().min(2).max(50),
  customerPhone: z.string().regex(/^\+?[\d\s-]+$/),
  serviceId: z.string().uuid(),
  barberId: z.string().uuid(),
  dateTime: z.coerce.date(),
});

export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  const body = await request.json();
  const result = bookingSchema.safeParse(body);
  
  if (!result.success) {
    return NextResponse.json(
      { success: false, errors: result.error.errors },
      { status: 400 }
    );
  }
  
  // Use result.data (validated)
}
```
